ee candidates, unless we release one before allocating to shift_candidate_beta. But we need the other three to be dispatched; after they are dispatched, their vehicles become available again. So we could allocate vehicle to shift_candidate_beta after we have dispatched the other three, freeing up a vehicle. However we need shift_candidate_beta prepared before we can stage it; staging occurs before we need to dispatch the others? Actually we need to stage shift_candidate_beta before goal; we can stage after we have dispatched the others, as long as we have vehicle available to allocate to shift_candidate_beta for preparation. So order: first handle shift_candidate_alpha, origin, destination (create, allocate vehicle, prepare, etc., dispatch them). After they are dispatched, vehicles become available. Then we can allocate a vehicle to shift_candidate_beta, prepare, assign operator, skill, stage. That would use only one vehicle for shift_candidate_beta, which we have available after the three dispatches. Good.

